# M-held-bytes, panel 124 (ratified 2026-09-09), closing defect 024's witness.
#
# The C side KEEPS the pointer past the call and reads it later. Written with
# a lend, `stash_put(s: label.cstr())`, this printed 0 where 13 is right and was
# a heap-use-after-free under `--sanitize`, because a lend's bytes die when its
# site runs again — iteration n+1 freed iteration n's. A lease is a COPY the
# program owns until `end_lease(@label)`, so C reads live bytes and the cell is
# emptied when the program says. Three iterations, three correct lengths, and
# the leak gate green at exit because every `.lease()` met its `end_lease`.

extern "lease-c-keeps-the-pointer.h"
    function stash_put(s: cstr)
    function stash_len() -> u64

function main()
    at: i64 @ 0

    while at < 3
        label: cstr @ ("row-" + at.to_str() + "-payload").lease()
        stash_put(s: label)
        print(stash_len())
        end_lease(@label)
        at @ at + 1
